  "final_message": "The bug was the classic mutable default argument: `tags=[]` is created once at function definition, so every call omitting `tags` appended to the same shared list. Replaced it with the `None` sentinel pattern (`tags=None` \u2192 `tags = []` inside the body), which gives each call a fresh list while still honoring an explicitly supplied list. `remove_tag` is untouched; the test passes (1/1 OK).\n\nDONE: Fixed `add_tag` mutable default in `tag_util.py` by using `tags=None` and creating a fresh list per call; `test_public.py` passes.",
